Gwen took 41 pictures at the zoo and 29 pictures at the museum. To find the total number of pictures she took, add the two together: 41 + 29 = 70. Then, she deleted 15 of the pictures. To find out how many pictures she has left, subtract 15 from the total number of pictures: 70 - 15 = 55. She still has 55 pictures from her vacation. 
\boxed{55}
